# WHAT THIS FILE IS. The template for `$HOME/.env` — the deploying user's
# home-directory credential file, outside every checkout (smoke-production-
# spec.md §3). It is never a repo-root `.env`: a fresh checkout has only this
# example, and `bun smoke` / `bun run migrate` read no env file from the
# checkout (they run with `--no-env-file`).
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE KEYS $HOME/.env HOLDS — EXACTLY THESE, AND NOTHING ELSE (§3, D52)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   "It holds exactly these keys and nothing else: the remote connection (host,
#    port, dbname); the runtime role passwords `rm_app`, `rm_worker` and
#    `rm_readonly`; `RM_ENV`; and `RM_CREDENTIALS`. It must not contain
#    `rm_owner`, `doadmin`, a superuser token, a service token, a signing key or
#    a model key; preflight enforces the list (§7 check 4)."
#
# Check 4 is an ALLOWLIST (backend/src/db/preflight.ts ENV_FILE_ALLOWED_KEYS):
# any other key WARNS under RM_ENV=stage and REFUSES the boot under RM_ENV=prod,
# and an rm_owner, doadmin or superuser line is named as what it is. The
# connection keys are spelled as the DigitalOcean connection panel prints them
# (`host`, `port`, `database` — `dbname` is accepted too — and `sslmode`), and a
# role line is `<role name> = <that role's password>`: scripts/lib/env-role.ts
# `urlForRole` assembles exactly one postgres:// URL per role from them.
#
# Where everything that is NOT in this file lives:
#   rm_owner      typed at the terminal by the one run that needs it (`bun run
#                 migrate`, a remote `bun smoke --migrate` or `--seed`) and never
#                 stored (§3). A `bun smoke --local` instance generates its own
#                 four role passwords in its state directory instead (§5).
#   doadmin       cluster provisioning only (§3, §9.1): typed where a §9.1 step
#                 needs it, never here.
#   service tokens  the API's automation-token store and a per-instance,
#                 per-holder token file in the instance's state directory (§3).
#   signing keys, bearer tokens, model keys  each participant's own entry in
#                 credential.json, which RM_CREDENTIALS points at (§6.1).
#   OPENCODE_API_KEY  exported in the shell of the one command that spends it
#                 (a rehearsal, CI's repository secret) — never this file.
#   everything else  the process environment of the program that reads it; the
#                 containers get theirs from the stack configuration, never from
#                 this file (see the reference section below).
#
# Any `bun smoke --local blank|dump|volume` mode ignores every remote connection
# value here (§3, §5). With no `--local` flag, `bun smoke` runs the stack against
# the server named here: the api as rm_app, the pipeline worker as rm_worker,
# every host-side read (the target lock, the identity read, preflight) as
# rm_readonly. It migrates only with `--migrate` and seeds only with `--seed`.

# --- $HOME/.env (a remote rehearsal or production host) ---------------------
host = db-rm-app-x.do-user-12345-0.b.db.ondigitalocean.com
port = 25060
database = defaultdb
sslmode = require
rm_app = <the rm_app role's password>
rm_worker = <the rm_worker role's password>
rm_readonly = <the rm_readonly role's password>
# prod on the production host; stage everywhere else (§4.1). The process
# environment's RM_ENV, when set, wins over this line.
RM_ENV = stage
RM_CREDENTIALS = /home/<user>/credential.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# credential.json — the roster, NOT a database role and NOT this file (§6.1)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The committee a host runs is the CONTENTS of `credential.json`, pointed to by
# RM_CREDENTIALS above (or `--credentials <path>`, which wins over it). Agents
# and judges are separate namespaces; each entry carries that participant's
# member id, signing key, API bearer token and model key, and each container
# receives only its own entry:
#     {
#       "agents": { "athena": { … }, "noop-analyst": { … }, "robot-money": { … } },
#       "judges": { "themis": { … } }
#     }
# Never the smoke fixture's committed, deliberately-public dev keys
# (scripts/lib/swarm/persona-keys.ts); never committed with real keys; never
# named credential.json inside the repo checkout itself. A rehearsal never reads
# a real credential.json: `--spoof-keys` writes a separate, instance-scoped
# generation and refuses to write to the path RM_CREDENTIALS names (§6.4).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REFERENCE — PROCESS ENVIRONMENT, NEVER $HOME/.env
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below is documentation of variables the BACKEND PROCESSES read from
# their own environment. None of it belongs in $HOME/.env (check 4 refuses it
# there on prod). `bun smoke` hands the containers what they need through the
# stack configuration (scripts/stack/config.ts buildComposeEnv — RM_ENV, the
# role URLs, the tokens) and the short passthrough allowlist
# (scripts/lib/smoke-compose-passthrough.ts); a host-side `bun run` of a backend
# program reads its own shell. Every line is commented out on purpose.
#
# There are no POSTGRES_USER / POSTGRES_PASSWORD / POSTGRES_DB lines: the local
# Postgres a `--local` boot starts is the stack's own, its superuser is used
# once to create the four roles and the database (§7.3), and the runtime roles'
# passwords are generated per instance.

# --- Host ports: DELIBERATELY NOT SET ANYWHERE -------------------------------
# WEB_PORT and POSTGRES_PORT are not configuration. Every published host port is
# assigned by Docker at start (scripts/stack/ports.ts), and a pinned one caused
# a real outage: an operator's copy pinned the api to exactly the port
# cloudflared routes stage.robotmoney-labs.dev to, and CI raced it. `bun smoke`
# warns and ignores either if it finds them. The one sanctioned pin is the CLI
# argument `bun smoke --static-port`, which fails (never falls back) when the
# tunnel's port is held. API_PORT is the container-internal port and is
# unconfigurable by construction.

# --- Runtime --------------------------------------------------------------
# RM_ENV — the §4.1 POLICY: prod | stage (see the $HOME/.env section above).
# A backend process also starts under `ephemeral` (tests) or `smoke`
# (development); both are refused as deployment policies (§4.3). Fail-closed:
# UNSET defaults to "prod" inside a process, and an unrecognized value refuses
# to start. Only "ephemeral" (or RM_ALLOW_INSECURE=1) opens privileged
# endpoints without a token.
# Allow privileged endpoints WITHOUT a token (onboarding/admin/analytics). Only
# for local throwaway demos — NEVER on a reachable box; provide tokens instead.
# RM_ALLOW_INSECURE=1
# Trust X-Forwarded-For for client-ip (rate limiting) — set ONLY when behind a
# known reverse proxy/edge. Off by default (uses the socket peer).
# TRUST_PROXY=1
# Origins allowed to call this API cross-origin (issue #871: split-repo
# frontend deployed as its own container, no longer same-origin). Comma-
# separated, no trailing slash. Empty by default — the single-box same-origin
# deployment (D11/D13) needs no CORS headers at all.
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://swarm.robotmoney.net

# --- Handle/id namespace boot guard (issue #602) --------------------------
# The api refuses to serve a database in which one member's handle is another
# member's id (`/swarm/members/<name>` would address two members). Both knobs
# below are passed into the api container by docker-compose.yml's api
# `environment:` block, so setting them in the deploy environment works;
# BOTH ARE UNSET HERE ON PURPOSE — the guard is fail-closed and its default
# budget is correct. Guard behavior and controls: D34 in docs/decisions.md.
# Adopted deployment preflight: docs/technical/smoke-production-spec.md
# (approved design; implementation not yet shipped).
#
# Emergency escape hatch: serve a VIOLATING database anyway (loudly, and
# reported as handle_namespace:"overridden" at /health). Set only to restore
# service while the rows are repaired, then UNSET it — while it is set, the
# guard is disarmed for every future boot, including the next bad restore.
# RM_ALLOW_HANDLE_NAMESPACE_VIOLATION=1
# The guard's wall-clock budget, an integer count of MILLISECONDS (default
# 8000; write "15000", never "15s" — a value that is not a positive integer of
# milliseconds within 2147483647 is ignored, loudly, and the default is used).
# PG_NAMESPACE_GUARD_TIMEOUT_MS=8000

# --- Worker ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Execution lane (REQUIRED per worker process, issue #107): one of
# analytics | research | generic. Empty/unknown fails loudly at startup.
# docker-compose.yml pins one container per lane; see
# backend/src/worker/lanes.ts. (There is no session lane: issue #1026 moved
# session timing out of the queue into the `system-scheduler` container.)
# WORKER_LANE=generic
# Owner id recorded in jobs.locked_by. Defaults to <lane>-<pid> (lane-aware).
# WORKER_ID=analytics-1
# JOB_VISIBILITY_TIMEOUT=300
# A live handler renews its lease on this cadence so long jobs are never reaped
# while their owner is alive. Default: a third of JOB_VISIBILITY_TIMEOUT.
# JOB_LEASE_RENEW_MS=100000
# Bounded shutdown: max wait for an in-flight job before it is released back to
# pending on SIGINT/SIGTERM.
# WORKER_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# The worker's database role is rm_worker, and a stack hands it BOTH of the
# worker's pools (DATABASE_URL and WORKER_DATABASE_URL) from its own role URLs
# (docker-compose.yml x-worker-env) — there is no fallback to the api's login.
# A host-side `bun run` of the worker sets both in its own shell.
# WORKER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://rm_worker:...@localhost:5432/robotmoney
# Where the worker's analytics updater submits computed outputs (issue #106):
# the authenticated /api/analytics/* boundary on the api process. Defaults to
# http://localhost:8787; docker-compose points it at http://api:8787.
# ANALYTICS_API_URL=http://localhost:8787

# --- Privileged endpoints -------------------------------------------------
# Guards member onboarding (/api/swarm/apply admin path + /register), admin
# lifecycle (/api/swarm/admin/*), AND the /admin task-queue jobs dashboard
# (/api/admin/*). If set, callers must send it as `X-Admin-Token` (required in
# every env). If unset, those endpoints are locked UNLESS RM_ALLOW_INSECURE=1 /
# RM_ENV=ephemeral. Set this on any reachable box. (The `bun run demo` TUI
# generates a fresh random value per launch and shows it in the interactive TUI.)
# ADMIN_TOKEN=
# Credential for the analytics-provider role. ONLY this role may write
# analytics data (POST /api/swarm/regime + every /api/analytics/* route),
# presented as a Bearer token. Same fail-closed rule as ADMIN_TOKEN. The worker
# uses the SAME value as its client credential and refuses to boot in demo/prod
# without it (never accept ADMIN_TOKEN or member bearers as substitutes).
# ANALYTICS_TOKEN=

# --- Passkey (WebAuthn) relying party --------------------------------------
# Only needed when a TLS-terminating proxy (e.g. cloudflared) sits in front of
# the api's plain-HTTP Bun server. Without these, relyingParty() in
# backend/src/api/routes/admin-webauthn.ts falls back to the request's own
# url.origin, which is http://... even though the browser's real origin is
# https://... — every passkey ceremony then fails origin verification. Set
# WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN to the public HTTPS origin the browser actually sees; leave
# WEBAUTHN_RP_ID unset unless the relying party's hostname must differ from
# that origin's hostname.
# WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN=https://robotmoney.network
# WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=robotmoney.network

# --- AUM producer build identity ------------------------------------------
# Passed by every backend Compose build into backend/Dockerfile. Set it to the
# exact source revision being built (normally `git rev-parse HEAD`). Blank or
# unset remains blank inside the image and is recorded by future snapshot
# publishers as producer_revision_status='unavailable'; no package version,
# timestamp, branch, or "unknown" fallback is fabricated.
# AUM_PRODUCER_REVISION=

# --- Swarm public origin ------------------------------------------------
# Absolute origin every link into the site is built from: the application
# status page (/swarm/apply/<memberId>) and the member profile. Defaults to
# https://robotmoney.network. Set it on any staging or local deployment, or your
# testers will be sent to production, where the member ids they just created do
# not exist.
#
# There is NO swarm onboarding email. The three mail settings that used to sit
# in this block were removed with the feature (issue #1026 W5, decision D50
# reversing D30); a deployment that still sets them is setting nothing.
# SWARM_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://robotmoney.network

# --- Session scheduling (issue #1026) --------------------------------------
# THERE IS NOTHING HERE TO SET, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN. A subject's epoch
# duration is the whole schedule: it is a column on the subject, set by the
# bootstrap data in the schema snapshot on a BLANK database, and changed
# afterwards only through the admin API as an ordinary authenticated update
# (docs/technical/system-scheduler-spec.md §2.2 and §2.3 — "No environment
# variable sets it. No seed command sets it. No boot overwrites it on a
# populated database."). There is no on/off state either (§2.4): a subject that
# must stop running epochs is deactivated through the same API.
#
# This block used to hold an enable flag and six cron/window variables. They
# are gone with the mechanism they configured; docs/technical/
# smoke-production-spec.md §6.3: "There is nothing to enable … There are no
# schedule rows, no cron strings, no `next_run_at`, and no enable command."
# A rehearsal that wants short epochs on a copy of production changes the
# subjects through the admin API, exactly as production would.

# --- system-scheduler (issue #1026) ----------------------------------------
# The clock container. It holds ONE credential — an API automation token — and
# no database role password, no signing key, no model key and no Docker socket
# (system-scheduler-spec.md §7).
#
# Where it dials the API. Inside compose this is the service name and
# docker-compose.yml already sets it; set it here only for a host-side
# `bun run scripts/system-scheduler.ts`.
# SCHEDULER_API_URL=http://api:8787
#
# PATH to the automation token, never the token itself. smoke-production-spec.md
# §3: the secret is "a file the boot places in the instance's state directory,
# named per instance, never in `~/.env` and never in the image". Putting the
# token in this file would be the one placement that paragraph forbids; this
# variable names where the boot already wrote it. Rotation is a re-provision
# plus a container restart, with no edit here.
# SCHEDULER_TOKEN_FILE=/run/rm-state/<instance>-scheduler-token
# Port the scheduler serves /health on (default 8090). It answers 200 when
# ready per smoke-production-spec.md §6.3 and 503 with the reason otherwise.
# SCHEDULER_HEALTH_PORT=8090

# SWARM_SEED_ROSTER=1 — seat the LIVE house roster (Athena, Robot Money) with
# the profile copy the committed manifests under
# frontend/public/data/swarm/manifests/members/ publish. Read by
# backend/src/db/seed.ts, so one `SWARM_SEED_ROSTER=1 bun run migrate` applies
# it; idempotent, and a re-run is how corrected manifest copy reaches a live
# deployment. OFF by default so CI, `bun run demo` and dev seeds are unchanged
# (the demo's own roster comes from backend/src/demo/e2e.ts). Additive only: it
# never touches a member outside the roster, and never writes a credential or
# applied_at/activated_at — a seeded member holds no token until an operator
# issues one through the normal admin path.
# SWARM_SEED_ROSTER=1

# SWARM_SEED_ROSTER_PRUNE=1 — the CONVERGENCE half of the above: retire every
# ACTIVE member that is not on the live roster (status='inactive'; rows are
# never deleted, so archived sessions keep resolving their participants by
# member id). Read only INSIDE the SWARM_SEED_ROSTER block, so it does nothing
# on its own and can never retire the roster without also seating it. It is a
# separate flag because it is the only half that can sweep away an operator
# legitimately admitted through the real apply flow — including woon, whom the
# v0 archive backfill seats. Members still in status='applied' are untouched,
# so a pending application survives for the admin to approve. Set it for the
# one convergence run on a deployment demo drivers have populated, not in the
# standing config.
# SWARM_SEED_ROSTER_PRUNE=1

# --- Analytics data source ------------------------------------------------
# ANALYTICS_SOURCE — the SINGLE authoritative selector for the analytics
# orchestrator (backend/src/analytics/index.ts::resolveAnalyticsSource, called by
# api + worker). Fail-closed: an unrecognized value refuses to start.
#   unset / live → real keyless fetchers (production AND demo default)
#   hermetic     → deterministic offline seeded source (CI backend unit tests +
#                  an explicit local-debug override; never a demo default)
# The legacy PROVIDER / analyticsProvider knob is DEPRECATED for source selection
# and no longer influences the live/demo path — do not use it to opt into real data.
# ANALYTICS_SOURCE=hermetic
# ANALYTICS_FLOOR_SEED=1 — one-time cold-DB raw-floor seed on a fresh live boot so
# it doesn't re-fetch years of history (esp. ~200 SEC-EDGAR requests) before the
# first classify. Idempotent/append-only (no-op once warm). Off by default.
# ANALYTICS_FLOOR_SEED=1
# FLOOR_SEED_PATH — override the vendored floor-seed file (must be readable here).
# FLOOR_SEED_PATH=
# EDGAR/MNA seed (issue #108): the committed
# backend/tests/fixtures/regime/edgar-mna-seed.csv.gz + .manifest.json cover
# 2010-01 through a pinned as-of month for the late-cycle MNA input.
# `bun run edgar-seed:bootstrap` (ANALYTICS_API_URL + ANALYTICS_TOKEN required)
# ingests it once and enables the research.refresh schedule; `edgar-seed:repopulate`
# restores missing rows on an existing DB; `edgar-seed:regenerate` (no
# credentials — EDGAR's full-text-search API is keyless) is the ONLY way the
# committed pair is produced/replaced, run explicitly by an operator, never in
# migrations/boot/CI. EDGAR_SEED_PATH/EDGAR_SEED_MANIFEST_PATH override the
# committed pair's location (tests only; must be readable here).
# EDGAR_SEED_PATH=
# EDGAR_SEED_MANIFEST_PATH=
# Capability-specific cache TTLs. Production defaults are HTTP off and
# token-price 30 seconds. The shared demo/smoke toolchain supplies one hour.
# These settings are not secrets.
# HTTP_FETCH_CACHE_TTL_MS=0
# TOKEN_PRICE_CACHE_TTL_MS=30000
# FETCH_CACHE_DIR only overrides the HTTP cache directory.
# FETCH_CACHE_DIR=

# --- Projects data source ---------------------------------------------------
# PROJECTS_SOURCE — selector for the /projects directory pipelines
# (backend/src/projects/access/select.ts::selectProjectsDataSource).
#   unset → vendored offline fixture source (demo/dev default; the ephemeral CI
#           env is ALWAYS hermetic, even if this leaks in)
#   live  → real keyless providers (CoinGecko / DexScreener / Base RPC)
# FAIL-CLOSED IN PROD: the projects pipelines REQUIRE an explicit
# PROJECTS_SOURCE=live under RM_ENV=prod and throw otherwise — fixture data is
# never served as production data — so every prod deployment must set:
# PROJECTS_SOURCE=live
#
# discoverProjects() under PROJECTS_SOURCE=live serves the COMMITTED v0-roster
# seed (backend/src/projects/seed/v0-roster-data.json), loaded network-free —
# no env var is needed to READ it. ROSTER_SEED_PATH/ROSTER_SEED_MANIFEST_PATH
# override its location (tests only; must be readable here).
# ROSTER_SEED_PATH=
# ROSTER_SEED_MANIFEST_PATH=
#
# V0_ANALYTICS_SOURCE_URL / V0_ANALYTICS_SOURCE_KEY — ONLY needed to
# REGENERATE that committed seed (`bun run projects-roster-seed:regenerate`,
# backend/scripts/projects-roster-seed-regenerate.ts): read-only anon-key
# access to v0's Supabase REST API, same 6-table scope R11 used (docs/audits/
# v0-v1-parity/R11-projects-supabase-audit.md). Never required at runtime —
# an operator sets these transiently in their own shell, never in a committed
# file, and never in a normal API/worker/demo deployment.
# V0_ANALYTICS_SOURCE_URL=
# V0_ANALYTICS_SOURCE_KEY=

# --- Vault economics (live Base RPC, issue #40) ---------------------------
# BASE_RPC_URL — Base mainnet (chainId 8453) JSON-RPC endpoint for the
# read-only vault-economics eth_call pipeline (backend/src/chain). Defaults to
# the public https://mainnet.base.org if unset.
# BASE_RPC_URL=
#
# --- The SHARED Base RPC rate budget, and the self-healing backfill (#709) ---
# BASE_RPC_MAX_CALLS_PER_SEC — the ONE token bucket every chain read in the app
# draws from: the per-minute wallet samplers, the vault/buyback readers, and the
# gap-repair backfill alike. There is deliberately no second limiter anywhere:
# the public Base RPC meters PER-IP, so an independent limiter for the backfill
# would sum to 2x against one bucket and 429 both — which is how the 2026-08-10
# storm killed vault.sample_share_price (issue #651). Note that
# BASE_RPC_MAX_CONCURRENCY is NOT this: it bounds how many requests are in
# flight, and on a worker lane that claims one job at a time in-flight never
# exceeds 1, so it paces nothing.
#
# UNSET (the default) means PACED at a conservative built-in rate of 0.25
# calls/s with a burst of 5 — roughly half the ~0.55 calls/s refill measured
# against https://mainnet.base.org (docs/technical/markets-asset-pricing-ingest.md §3.4),
# and ~7.5x what the live per-minute samplers actually draw (~0.033 calls/s).
# Base publishes no rate limit for its public endpoint — the docs say only that
# it is "rate-limited and not suitable for production traffic" — so this is a
# deliberately safe guess rather than a vendor figure, and the limiter corrects
# itself downward anyway: a 429 or a JSON-RPC -32016 drains the bucket.
#
# Because pacing is on by default, the self-healing backfill is ON by default
# too: ops.repair_gaps dispatches wallet AUM / sleeve gap repair on a live
# deployment without any configuration. That is the point of #709.
#
# SET IT if you have measured your own deployment's real budget — a keyed
# provider's endpoint will take far more than 0.25/s and the backfill converges
# proportionally faster.
# BASE_RPC_MAX_CALLS_PER_SEC=
#
# SET IT TO 0 to turn pacing off entirely (the pre-v0.3.0 transport). That is
# the explicit opt-out and it also stops the backfill: ops.repair_gaps refuses
# to dispatch rather than sweep unpaced. An unreadable value is NOT an opt-out —
# it falls back to the default, so a typo cannot silently unpace production.
#
# BASE_RPC_RATE_BURST — bucket capacity (default: 5, the measured provider
# bucket depth; a burst of 1 would serialize even a single wallet sample, which
# costs 2 eth_calls).
# BASE_RPC_RATE_BURST=
# WALLET_BACKFILL_MAX_DAYS_PER_RUN — blast-radius cap per dispatcher run
# (default 10). A wider gap closes over successive hourly runs; what a run
# deferred is reported in its job_runs output, never silently dropped.
# WALLET_BACKFILL_MAX_DAYS_PER_RUN=
# WALLET_BACKFILL_MAX_ATTEMPTS_PER_DAY — how many times an unrepairable day is
# retried before it is left alone (default 3). An exhausted day remains a
# DISCLOSED gap in GET /api/admin/gaps; it is never interpolated.
# WALLET_BACKFILL_MAX_ATTEMPTS_PER_DAY=
# GECKO_MIN_INTERVAL_MS — minimum spacing between GeckoTerminal requests, spot
# and daily-OHLCV alike (default 6000, i.e. <=10 req/min, the keyless per-IP
# quota). One serializer covers both paths (backend/src/chain/gecko-rate-limit.ts)
# because they share that quota. A keyless 429 was observed on the 6th call in
# ~15s. This is a GeckoTerminal control and has nothing to do with the RPC
# budget. GECKO_OHLCV_MIN_INTERVAL_MS is the superseded historical-path name and
# is still read as a fallback.
# GECKO_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=
# VAULT_ADDRESS / USDC_ADDRESS — default to the documented RobotMoneyVault +
# Base USDC addresses (see docs/skill/installation.html); override only for a
# different deployment.
# VAULT_ADDRESS=
# USDC_ADDRESS=
# ADAPTER_MORPHO_ADDRESS / ADAPTER_AAVE_ADDRESS / ADAPTER_COMPOUND_ADDRESS —
# the three adapter contract addresses. NOT auto-discovered on-chain (decision
# D15) — the REAL deployed Base mainnet adapter addresses are the built-in
# defaults (backend/src/config.ts resolveVaultAdapters, since PR #112), so a
# deployment with only DATABASE_URL set reads real per-adapter TVL. Override
# only for a re-pointed deployment.
# ADAPTER_MORPHO_ADDRESS=
# ADAPTER_AAVE_ADDRESS=
# ADAPTER_COMPOUND_ADDRESS=

# --- Real inference (OpenCode Zen) ----------------------------------------
# OPENCODE_API_KEY — the OpenCode Zen API key (https://opencode.ai/zen). This is
# the opencode CLI's own env var name (fixed by the provider definition on
# models.dev), so a locally-spawned opencode inherits it with no forwarding.
# Used by every real-inference path: swarm take authorship
# (scripts/lib/swarm/inference.ts), the member-agent onboarding containers
# (scripts/lib/onboarding-eval.ts), and the contribution-advisory reviewer.
#
# ONE name, DIFFERENT value per environment — so spend is attributable and
# rotating one key never touches another:
#     CI     → repository secret OPENCODE_API_KEY
#     Stage  → exported in the shell of the command that spends it
#     Local  → exported in your own shell, your own key
# NEVER $HOME/.env: §3 keeps model keys out of it (check 4), and a participant's
# model key is its own credential.json entry.
#
# Zen bills the key from pay-as-you-go credit on its workspace. It is NOT
# covered by an opencode subscription ("Go" funds the CLI/app, not this key):
# an unfunded key authenticates fine but returns `CreditsError: Insufficient
# balance` on every paid model. To run with no key at all, select a keyless
# model with AGENT_MODEL=free (see below).
# OPENCODE_API_KEY=
#
# --- Consensus judge (issue #752) -----------------------------------------
# The judge EXPLAINS, it does not DECIDE: it authors a session's rationale,
# disagreements and release-safety opinion, and it never authors a weight. The
# vector always comes from meanTakeWeights() in backend/src/swarm/domain.ts.
#
# NOTHING FOR THE JUDGE IS CONFIGURED HERE. The judge is a participant (smoke
# spec §6.2, D52): a standing container that takes its signing key, bearer
# token and model key from its credential.json entry, never from this file and
# never from `api`. Its on/off switch and model are `swarm_judge_config` rows,
# written only over POST /api/swarm/admin/judge. SWARM_JUDGE_BASE_URL and
# SWARM_JUDGE_TIMEOUT_MS used to be set here for an inline judge inside `api`;
# no service reads them from this environment any more.
#
# AGENT_MODEL — which agent to run. ONE selector; the model ids themselves live
# in scripts/lib/model-registry.ts, so changing what `deepseek` means is a code
# review, not an untracked `export`. Accepted forms:
#     <family>          e.g. deepseek   → that family's pinned default
#     <family>/<model>  e.g. kimi/k2.6  → that exact model
#     opencode/<id>                     → raw escape hatch, unvalidated
#     unset                             → repo default (opencode/deepseek-v4-flash)
# Families: deepseek, kimi, claude, gpt, glm, minimax, qwen, grok, gemini, free.
# An unknown family or model FAILS LOUDLY rather than falling back.
# Note: `claude/*` on Zen carries a coding-assistant framing that refuses the
# swarm-take persona — fine for agentic work, unreliable for authoring.
# AGENT_MODEL=

# --- Secrets (added in later phases) -------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# FRED_API_KEY=
